msgstr "Actomyosin are simple muscle structures that cell colonies can use to more effectively pull them in a direction or rotate. They are not available for wall-type membranes as they rely on flex of the colony to function. And as a result of that, they are most effective when there's just one per cell but many cells in a colony have this organelle."

